index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bc4bd467c4217e77f7214735453c16b0e7abfd34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/results/codex/final_heldout_audit/report.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+**Verdict: VALID WITH CAVEATS.** The saved artifacts reproduce the preregistered primary result: v4 is non-inferior to matched GUI-Owl at the −6.9 pp margin, under the specified rerun and nominal inference rules. Superiority over GUI-Owl is not established. No P1 defect or erroneous primary count was substantiated. Device-state isolation is imperfect, one reference-arm success has a destructive extra action, and the analysis input guard is weaker than its identity claim.
+
+Offline audit of all specified inputs, including the entire preregistration and every dated entry; 1,044 original episodes, 122 reruns, exception traces, execution/server/queue/guard logs, runners, agents and local harness patches. No AndroidWorld, emulator, llama-server or adb was run; no process was signalled. All writes are in this audit directory. [Independent code](recompute.py), [723 output checks](published_numeric_checks.json), [complete numerical tables](numbers.md), [execution review](execution_review.md), and [all 88 success reviews](success_review.md) provide the supporting detail.
+
+**Findings**
+
+- **P2-1 — App snapshot restoration was skipped, so equal device configuration does not establish equal starting state.** `task_eval.py:116–125` catches snapshot restoration errors and proceeds. `app_snapshot.py:91–107` raises before clearing/copying app data when the snapshot is missing. The v4/1234 rerun log contains **263** “Snapshot not found” skips; ordinary full runs show approximately 271–275, across both devices and all arms. This is a shared harness limitation, not a special change benefiting the reruns. Actual state carryover is visible: v1/2026 attempts to create Thomas Pereira at 10:21, and that contact is still present in OpenAppTaskEval at 11:21. Evidence: [log at contact creation](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/androidworld_sealed/v1_seed2026/run_output.SEALED.log:10174), [later skipped restore](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/results/androidworld_sealed/v1_seed2026/run_output.SEALED.log:50476), [trajectory](trajectory_80_1.jpg), [all snapshot warnings with locations](execution_logs.json). Task-specific DB clearing and Clock resets still run; this does **not** mean every generated task state was wrong. It does mean preferences/residual state and episode order are not fully controlled, including when 113 episodes move to the other device. Neither the direction nor magnitude of resulting bias can be identified from these artifacts. Disclose this limitation; future runs need verified state restoration. Cross-template carryover is also outside what clustering only by template can account for.
+
+- **P2-2 — A reference-arm “open Contacts” success includes deleting a contact.** v1/2026 OpenAppTaskEval opens Contacts, selects all, presses trash, confirms deletion, then reports complete. The final screen says “No contacts yet” and “1 contact deleted.” [Source checker](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/android_world/android_world/task_evals/single/system.py:484) checks only the foreground package, so the unrelated deletion is unpenalized. The literal open-app condition is satisfied, but this is not a clean user-level success. See [review #80](success_review.md) and [screens](trajectory_80_1.jpg). Added one proposal to [disputes_proposed.json](disputes_proposed.json); the original dispute file is untouched. Counting this proposal as failure changes v1 to **31/348**, and v4−v1 to **+6.61 pp**, CI **[1.54, 11.70]**, p **0.0119**. It does not affect v4−GUI-Owl.
+
+- **P3-1 — Goal agreement is not an instance-identity check.** [Analysis loader](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/sealed_analysis.py:44) does not validate stored `seed` or `instance_id`; [replacement admission](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/scripts/sealed_analysis.py:138) checks any original exception, not specifically eligible setup failures or information-retrieval date rewording. A fixture using the actual v4/2026 TasksDueNextWeek artifact passes the v4/1234 goal predicate despite different instance seeds. A separate fixture with altered seed/instance metadata also passes the new nine-date-case fallback. These are audit-only admission demonstrations, **not observed substitutions**: [counterexamples](validator_counterexample.json). Independent checks found no wrong instance among the actual reruns. Validate the derived instance seed, instance ID and eligible phase explicitly; retain the documented date exception rather than treating matching prose as sufficient proof.
+
+- **P3-2 — Two execution descriptions need correction; scores are unaffected.** The [16:20 entry](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:289) calls both VLC rerun crashes “in an agent step.” Their saved tracebacks instead show `episode_runner.py:76 -> agent.reset`, before its step loop. They still correctly count as failures because their one rerun was exhausted. Also, [13:40](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:276) promises exclusion of three **templates**, whereas published sensitivity B excludes seven individual **pairs**. The 16:20 description of B is accurate. I computed the literal three-template exclusion too: **54 versus 43 over 339 pairs/113 clusters**, +3.245 pp, CI [−3.030, 9.524], p 0.3655; NI remains established. See [tracebacks](exceptions.json) and [numbers](numbers.md).
+
+**Recomputed result and interpretation**
+
+| Arm | Seed 7 /116 | Seed 1234 /116 | Seed 2026 /116 | Pooled | Wilson 95%, % |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| v4 | 18 | 17 | 19 | 54/348 = 15.52% | 12.092–19.696 |
+| GUI-Owl matched | 16 | 13 | 18 | 47/348 = 13.51% | 10.311–17.498 |
+| v1 reference | 11 | 10 | 11 | 32/348 = 9.20% | 6.589–12.693 |
+
+Primary v4−GUI-Owl is **+2.011494 pp**, test-inversion 95% CI **[−4.477612, 8.510638]**, 10,000-draw p **0.6023398**. Published outward rounding [−4.5, 8.6] is correct. Independently enumerating the zero-null sign distribution gives p **0.5981847**, consistent with Monte Carlo variation. The lower bound exceeds −6.9, so the specified NI decision follows; the interval includes zero, so superiority does not.
+
+The correct preregistration reading is **116 template clusters, each containing its three seed instances** ([Analysis](/Users/alpha/lfm3-android/docs/PREREG_v4.md:39)). Treating 348 seed/template instances as independent clusters would discard the dependence the preregistration explicitly protects against. Per-seed v4-only/GUI-Owl-only/both counts are **15/13/3**, **13/9/4**, **11/10/8**; exact McNemar p values are **0.8505540**, **0.5234671**, **1.0**. All per-seed/pooled Wilson values, other comparisons, answer/action/difficulty breakdowns, secondary denominators and the seed-7 analysis reproduce; see [numbers.md](numbers.md).
+
+The 78 goal-text-varying templates give v4 **32/234**, GUI-Owl **33/234**, difference **−0.427 pp**, CI **[−8.108, 7.207]**: NI is **not** established for that subgroup. This does not overturn the preregistered all-template endpoint. Constant goal text also does not imply invariant hidden task state: the source manifest distinguishes 20 such templates. Seed 30 remains development data and is not pooled into the held-out result.
+
+| Sensitivity | Pairs / clusters | v4 / GUI-Owl successes | Difference pp | 95% CI, exact endpoints | NI |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|
+| B: drop remaining exception pairs | 341 /116 | 54 /44 | +2.933 | [−3.390, 9.290] | yes |
+| C: count the 113 v4/1234 reruns as failures | 348 /116 | 37 /47 | −2.874 | [−8.333, 2.614] | **no** |
+| D: exclude seed 1234, paired | 232 /116 | 37 /34 | +1.293 | [−5.769, 8.333] | yes |
+| Existing seed-7 stopwatch dispute | 348 /116 | 53 /47 | +1.724 | [−4.762, 8.205] | yes |
+
+The sensitivity files reproduce, including p values **0.4096 / 0.3616 / 0.8125** for B/C/D. The 16:20 entry fairly states the dependence on the rerun rule: C fails NI, while D shows the remaining two seeds can establish it. C is a deliberately different scoring rule, not evidence that the eligible reruns were improperly selected. The entry's “only one that fails” is correct among A–D, not a claim about every possible subgroup.
+
+**Execution and fairness conclusion**
+
+The **117 newly rerun originals qualify**, including all 113 v4/1234 device-setup crashes. BrowserDraw had already reached agent steps; the two specified SMS exceptions occurred in `is_successful`; all three correctly remain failures. All 122 reruns, including seed 7, have one logged start and one saved result each. Guards never fired. v1/2026's initial emulator-2 attempt had zero episodes, so the unchanged full relaunch on emulator 1 was legitimate. Every arm/device assignment, pause and resume is recorded in [execution_review.md](execution_review.md).
+
+The exhaustive midnight–10:05 emulator-2 timeline contains GUI-Owl/1234's last three episodes, five seed-7 reruns, v4/1234's 116 episodes, and the zero-episode v1 launch. The two pre-hang AudioRecorder failures have responsive screens and normal fetches; their actions do not justify an infrastructure exception. No additional saved episode was shown to be invalidated by the hang.
+
+Applying the one-rerun rule to 113 episodes is consistent and not outcome-selective merely because the number is large. Moving devices is nevertheless subject to P2-1. The 13-hour host delay is **not evidence of a later benchmark date**: task initialization resets AndroidWorld's date to **2023-10-15 15:34 UTC**, with task-specific adjustments; saved commands/screens corroborate this. Model/projector paths, context, runner/agent flags and AVD configuration agree with the specified arms. Historical model-byte identity and actual per-episode app-list equality cannot be certified because runtime hashes and complete prompts were not saved; no change was evidenced.
+
+The nine changed goals are all explained by `InformationRetrieval.initialize_task`: parent device setup occurs before seeded `_maybe_replace_date` at line 85. Every one matches both other arms' goal, has the correct saved instance seed, and **fails**, so admitting these nine does not add any success. All 1,037 stored instance seeds and all 1,166 instance IDs validate; exception files omit the seed and full hidden parameter dictionaries are not saved. The diff from `dd2f7f7` changes only the stated goal admission/annotation and stale “pending” note; statistical/scoring logic is unchanged. Details and all nine text changes are in the execution review.
+
+**Success validity and power limits**
+
+Reviewed all **88** new-seed successes: v4 36, GUI-Owl 31, v1 21. All have a terminal action; none succeeds solely on budget exhaustion. One new proposal is described above; 87 have no sufficient contradiction in the saved evidence. The seed-1234 lemongrass recipe successes are vacuous zero-target instances permitted by the generator, not demonstrated false positives. The calendar deletion with a stale-looking final search list has an explicit delete confirmation and a DB-checker success; the screenshot alone is insufficient to dispute it. [The ledger](success_review.md) distinguishes these cases and the limits of inspecting screenshots without complete saved databases.
+
+Sample size alone does not determine power. Using the observed between-template variance **as a planning approximation held fixed**, the cluster SE is **3.247 pp**, giving an approximately **9.10 pp** effect for 80% two-sided superiority power, and **56.6%** NI power at a true difference of zero with this −6.9 pp margin and the lower two-sided 95% bound rule. This is not an exact sign-flip power calculation or additional evidence for the observed effect; [calculation](power_approximation.json). Three seeds give 348 paired outcomes, not 348 independent template replications. The supplied shifted-sign-flip CI is nominal and assumes symmetry; pooled Wilson intervals are ordinary binomial summaries, not cluster-adjusted intervals. The supported claim is the stated conditional NI result in this harness, with rerun/state/checker caveats, not equivalence, superiority over GUI-Owl, or demonstrated NI on every task subset.
